// us.irc.core — the shared ontology of the Internal Revenue Code formalization
// (DECISION-0379, `docs/foundations/us-irc/PLAN.ru.md` §5.2, §6.1). This
// package pins NO statutory text of its own (no `sources.law` fragments) and
// carries NO rules: it declares only the types, roles, entities and relation
// SHAPES that every `us.irc.<leaf>` owner package imports. A local definition
// or a norm that PRODUCES a value of one of these types stays with its owner
// (§7701(a) general definitions live in `us.irc.definitions`; rates, filing
// statuses, classification tests stay with the subject-matter owner).
//
// WHY A SEPARATE PACKAGE FROM `us.irc.definitions`. Core answers "what KIND
// of thing is a taxpayer, a period, a dollar amount, a notice" — identity and
// shape. `us.irc.definitions` answers "which persons COUNT as a corporation
// for this title" — the §7701(a) classification tests themselves. Mixing the
// two would make every owner import classification logic it may not need yet,
// and would put a compiled rule where DECISION-0379 §1.1 forbids one.
//
// MODULE MAP
//   package.law                  — this file: header, module map, conventions
//   persons.law                  — Person and its §7701(a)(1) subtypes; Organ
//                                   and the named authorities (§7701(a)(11)-
//                                   (12)); legal roles (Taxpayer, Employer,
//                                   Employee, Fiduciary, WithholdingAgent,
//                                   Transferee, Payee)
//   time.law                     — TimeSpan/TaxableYear/Period (§441); the
//                                   federal business-day calendar is NOT here
//   money-and-liabilities.law    — TaxKind (one value per taxing chapter of
//                                   the snapshot), liability/payment shapes
//   documents-and-events.law     — Return, Notice, Assessment, Claim,
//                                   Election, Proceeding, Lien, Levy
//   property-and-attributes.law  — Asset/Lot, Transaction, OwnershipInterest,
//                                   TaxAttribute/Carryover
//
// CONVENTIONS (all modules)
//   * every symbol is `pub`: this package exists to be imported;
//   * `kind institutional` for a relation a RULE derives (an owner's norm
//     produces it); `kind empirical` for a relation a CASE asserts as a raw
//     fact. Core never chooses which one an owner's use will be — the choice
//     here reflects only the shape most owners will need (a case typically
//     ASSERTS that a return was filed on a date, so `filed_on` is empirical;
//     a case typically DERIVES a computed liability, so `liability` is
//     institutional). An owner is free to re-derive an "empirical" relation
//     institutionally inside its own package if its own text computes it —
//     that is a choice about the RULE, not about this shape;
//   * `label en official "…"` quotes the exact operative sentence of
//     §7701(a) or the cited procedural section where one names the concept
//     directly; `label en unofficial "…"` is used where the Code uses the
//     word without a dictionary definition (e.g. "employer", "payee");
//   * money is untyped-currency `Money` (bare, as `corpus/laws/us/leonard-v-
//     pepsico` and the KZ income-tax package use it for their own currency):
//     every amount in `us.irc.*` is USD by convention of the title itself,
//     never mixed with another currency, so a `Money<USD>` parameter would
//     add a type argument no scenario in this title will ever vary;
//   * no `@source` anchors in this package (§194 units are pinned by OWNERS,
//     not by core) — `source IRC_TITLE26` below identifies the title for
//     `[metadata].primarySource` only, and carries no edition/publication:
//     the pinned bytes of each section live in the owner that formalizes it
//     (`sources.law`, generated per-package by
//     `corpus/tools/sources/sync/sync_us_irc_fragments.py --package <leaf>`);
//   * a name that does not already exist in a neighbour package is added
//     here by the coordinator in the SAME change that a package needs it for
//     (`pub` at the owner, per `docs/PACKAGE-LAYOUT.ru.md`) — this file is
//     the shared surface, and it grows only additively (DECISION-0379 §1.1
//     "остаётся полномочием этого поручения").

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irc.core version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irc:core";

// Identifies Title 26 for `[metadata].primarySource` (`law.toml`). No
// `edition`/`publication`/`fragment` here: core pins no bytes. The pinned
// consolidated 2024 Edition and its Public Law patches are recorded, section
// by section, in each OWNER package's own `sources.law`
// (`docs/foundations/us-irc/PLAN.ru.md` §5.2 item 5; DECISION-0379 §1.3).
pub source IRC_TITLE26 {
    kind code;
    jurisdiction US;
    number "26 U.S.C.";
    label en official "Internal Revenue Code";
}
